# Built binary.
/picvert

# Rendered artefacts: regenerated from cv.json, never a source.
*.html
# (PDFs are artefacts, but the fonts below are not)
*.pdf
*.png

# ...except the interface, which is SOURCE that happens to be HTML. Without
# this exception a fresh clone builds a binary with nothing embedded in it, and
# the failure looks like a broken editor rather than a missing file.
!internal/server/web/*.html
!internal/server/web/**/*.html

# Real CVs. A profile carries a name, an address and an employer; the engine's
# default is that none of that is in the repository.
/data/

# Font subsets: generated by scripts/gen-webfonts.py from the .ttf beside them.
# Committed on purpose — see fonts/README.md — so that building needs no Python.

# Typechecking only. Building the interface needs Go and nothing else, so a
# clone without this is a clone that still builds and still runs — it just
# cannot tell you whether the types hold.
/node_modules/

# The bundled interface, under internal/server/web/assets, is generated by
# tools/bundle and COMMITTED on purpose — same rule as the font subsets above,
# so that a checkout builds with the Go toolchain alone. CI rebuilds it and
# fails if it differs, which is what keeps a committed artefact honest.

# The real configuration. It holds the Turnstile secret and the admin password
# hash, so it is never committed — deploy/picvert.yaml.example is the one that
# is, with placeholders. A secret in a repository is a secret that has to be
# rotated the moment anybody clones it.
/picvert.yaml
/*.local.yaml
